  "ExplanationWrongB": "Northfield's corporate beta of 1.15 reflects the systematic risk of its existing operations, not the technology project. When a firm enters a new business segment with different risk characteristics, the corporate beta is no longer representative. The technology segment has comparable firms with β = 1.70, indicating substantially higher systematic risk. Using the corporate beta (1.15) would understate the required return by 3.30%, encouraging overinvestment in risky projects. The pure-play method using comparable-company betas is the standard approach for project-specific cost of capital estimation.",
