  "ExplanationCorrect": "DIO = Average Inventory / (COGS/365) = $3.5M / ($25.55M/365) = $3.5M / $70,000 = 50.0 days. DSO = Average AR / (Revenue/365) = $3.8M / ($36.5M/365) = $3.8M / $100,000 = 38.0 days. DPO = Average AP / (COGS/365) = $3.08M / $70,000 = 44.0 days. CCC = DIO + DSO − DPO = 50 + 38 − 44 = 44 days. This means Avalon takes 44 days on average from paying suppliers for inventory to collecting cash from customers — the period during which the firm must finance its operations. A shorter CCC reduces the need for external financing and improves liquidity. The three levers to reduce CCC: reduce DIO (faster inventory turnover), reduce DSO (faster collection), or increase DPO (slower payment to suppliers). Each has trade-offs: aggressive DPO extension may damage supplier relationships or forfeit early payment discounts.",
  "ExplanationWrongA": "",
