  "ExplanationWrongC": "DIO of 35 days results from using revenue instead of COGS: $3.5M/($36.5M/365) = $3.5M/$100,000 = 35 days. Inventory is carried at cost on the balance sheet and flows through COGS on the income statement — the matching principle requires using COGS, not revenue, to compute inventory turnover. The correct DIO is 50 days, and the correct CCC is 44 days.",
